the job conclusion stays success while advisory' — this holds only for the contract step, not the surrounding checkout/install steps"],"finding":"The plan scopes `continue-on-error: ${{ inputs.advisory-mode }}` to the scanner CONTRACT step only, but the reusable scanner job (_scanner-integration.yml) runs checkout (checkout-gerrit-change-action), setup-python, setup-uv, and `uv sync --locked --extra dev` BEFORE that step. In advisory Stage A a failure in any of those infra steps makes the scanner JOB conclusion `failure`; im-open/workflow-conclusion observes all jobs in the run, so env.WORKFLOW_CONCLUSION becomes `failure`, and gerrit-verify.yaml's normalize step feeds env.WORKFLOW_CONCLUSION into CONCLUSION (the scanner is not in the route enumeration that would neutralize it) — casting Verified -1. That is precisely the vacuous-block class Stage A is designed to prevent, now reachable from a flaky Gerrit checkout or transient `uv sync` on an advisory job.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f60bb887b05a27d5d","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Scope section — 'apply continue-on-error: ${{ inputs.advisory-mode }} to the scanner contract step inside the reusable job'; and Anti-90c7 safety design","norm_id":"n473589c4829ca228","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Advisory Stage-A run where checkout-gerrit-change-action or `uv sync --locked` fails transiently on the scanner job while every route job passes","A patchset that predates scripts/install_review_scanners.py but where the contract step's own if-guard is bypassed by an earlier install failure"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follo